Package: pneumoalloc
Title: Serotype-Specific Pneumococcal Carriage with Multiple Serotype
    Carriage: A Unified Bayesian Framework
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Kaige", "Dong", , "kaige.dong@charite.de", role = c("aut", "cre"))
URL: https://github.com/lvyihongning/pneumoalloc
BugReports: https://github.com/lvyihongning/pneumoalloc/issues
Description: Estimates overall, multiple serotype and serotype-specific
    pneumococcal carriage prevalence, and their prevalence ratios across
    repeated cross-sectional surveys, when children can carry more than one
    serotype at a time. Carriage states (no carriage, one, two, three or
    more serotypes) and the types of multiple serotype carriage are
    estimated with multinomial-logit models. Serotype-specific prevalence
    is estimated with one joint model of overall carriage (logistic),
    serotype composition among carriers (fractional multinomial logit) and
    density among carriers (lognormal with a multiplicity sub-model), in
    all children or among children with multiple serotype carriage. Four
    approaches to allocating a multiple carriage episode among its
    serotypes (dominant serotype, equal share, relative abundance and
    serotype-specific density) differ only in the allocation weights, so
    they are compared on the same population, design and priors. All
    estimates are standardised over the study population. Models are
    fitted with 'Stan' through 'cmdstanr'.
